      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_unix_t_t_y_1a3fb4f048230f94368b8a7e857c7d5e64" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void UnixTTY::close</definition>
        <argsstring>() override</argsstring>
        <name>close</name>
        <qualifiedname>UnixTTY::close</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="class_t_t_y_1afc373cf592a31802ef4b11e48e81a7c0">close</reimplements>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Close the PTY and terminate the shell process. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Sequence:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>signalThreadShouldExit()</computeroutput> — ask the reader thread to stop.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>SIGKILL</computeroutput> child immediately — child death is the fastest path to unblock the reader&apos;s blocking <computeroutput><ref refid="class_unix_t_t_y_1a0f2c38d817e1c94759b38a832fa1ed0e" kindref="member">read()</ref></computeroutput>. SIGTERM grace is omitted because ARCHITECT requires instant kill on pane close.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Close master fd — causes the reader to see EOF if still in <computeroutput><ref refid="class_unix_t_t_y_1a0f2c38d817e1c94759b38a832fa1ed0e" kindref="member">read()</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>stopThread (<ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a7a82c07385a8151bb17399ea971a00bf" kindref="member">instantKillJoinTimeoutMs</ref>)</computeroutput> — bounded join on the reader.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>MESSAGE THREAD context.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Shutdown sequence</title><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>signalThreadShouldExit()</computeroutput> — ask the reader thread to stop.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>SIGKILL</computeroutput> child immediately — child death is the fastest path to unblock the reader&apos;s blocking <computeroutput><ref refid="class_unix_t_t_y_1a0f2c38d817e1c94759b38a832fa1ed0e" kindref="member">read()</ref></computeroutput>. SIGTERM grace is omitted because ARCHITECT requires instant kill on pane close.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Close master fd — causes the reader to see EOF if still in <computeroutput><ref refid="class_unix_t_t_y_1a0f2c38d817e1c94759b38a832fa1ed0e" kindref="member">read()</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>stopThread (<ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a7a82c07385a8151bb17399ea971a00bf" kindref="member">instantKillJoinTimeoutMs</ref>)</computeroutput> — bounded join on the reader.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>MESSAGE THREAD context. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
