        <briefdescription>
<para>Notify the kernel PTY of a new window size via ioctl and SIGWINCH. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Skipped if <computeroutput>cols</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>rows</computeroutput> are identical to the last successful call (guard on <computeroutput><ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a35127fabfe38b27ca01ad77f9f01e19b" kindref="member">lastResizeCols</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a71cd2443a214998931dc72983813b50a" kindref="member">lastResizeRows</ref></computeroutput>). When dims change:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Issues <computeroutput>ioctl (<ref refid="class_unix_t_t_y_1a89b2d5a9a85268a8376bb8b7adaa27e5" kindref="member">master</ref>, TIOCSWINSZ, &amp;ws)</computeroutput> to update the kernel&apos;s idea of the window size, including physical pixel dimensions so tools such as chafa can query cell and viewport pixel size via <computeroutput>CSI 14 t</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>CSI 16 t</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Sends <computeroutput>SIGWINCH</computeroutput> to the child process so the shell and any running TUI application can re-query the size.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Updates <computeroutput><ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a35127fabfe38b27ca01ad77f9f01e19b" kindref="member">lastResizeCols</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a71cd2443a214998931dc72983813b50a" kindref="member">lastResizeRows</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ws</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>New window size (cols, rows, pixel extents). Pass 0 for pixel extents when the display has not yet been calibrated.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>MESSAGE THREAD context. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
